  "worked_solution": "We isolate $x$ by applying the addition and multiplication principles, as usual.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & <\\frac{5x+7}{3}\\le 4 \\\\ -1\\cdot 3 & <\\frac{5x+7}{3}\\cdot 3\\le 4\\cdot 3 \\\\ -3 & <5x+7\\le 12 \\\\ -3-7 & <5x+7-7\\le 12-7 \\\\ -10 & <5x\\le 5 \\\\ \\frac{-10}{5} & <\\frac{5x}{5}\\le \\frac{5}{5} \\\\ -2 & <x\\le 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can represent this solution using a number line, as follows.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251228/assets/a70249a33b29eeec3c36c1077486fecfcdf19eb653973d41d19987be4a80be0a.png)",
